From: WL2GO
Subject: Report the current busy state to every newly attached host

UpdateBusyDetector emits BUSY TRUE/FALSE only on a transition, and
TCPSendCommandToHost silently drops anything sent while no host socket is
attached. A host that connects while the channel is already busy therefore
never learns it -- it sees nothing until the next transition, which for a
continuous carrier never comes.

WL2GO attaches a short-lived listener between modem spawn and Pat's dial to
require 10 consecutive clear seconds before transmitting; without an initial
state report, an already-busy channel would look clear for the whole window.
Pat's own waitIfBusy has the same edge-only gap, so this also makes its
busy-channel fallback see a pre-existing carrier.

Only DISC is reported because that is the only ProtocolState in which the
busy detector runs (UpdateBusyDetector returns early otherwise), so any
stored verdict from another state would be stale.

diff --git a/src/common/TCPHostInterface.c b/src/common/TCPHostInterface.c
index ecffe9b..fc083ea 100644
--- a/src/common/TCPHostInterface.c
+++ b/src/common/TCPHostInterface.c
@@ -46,6 +46,9 @@ int _memicmp(unsigned char *a, unsigned char *b, int n);
 // Defined in ARDOPC.c, set by --hostbind. Empty means INADDR_ANY.
 extern char HostBindAddr[64];
 
+// Current busy-detector verdict (ARDOPC.c); it has no header declaration.
+extern BOOL blnBusyStatus;
+
 #define GetBuff() _GetBuff(__FILE__, __LINE__)
 #define ReleaseBuffer(s) _ReleaseBuffer(s, __FILE__, __LINE__)
 #define Q_REM(s) _Q_REM(s, __FILE__, __LINE__)
@@ -679,6 +682,14 @@ void TCPHostPoll()
 				ioctl(TCPControlSock, FIONBIO, &param);
 				CONNECTED = TRUE;
 //				SendCommandToHost("RDY");
+
+				// BUSY TRUE/FALSE is otherwise sent only on a transition
+				// (UpdateBusyDetector), so a host that attaches while the
+				// channel is already busy would never hear about it. Tell
+				// every newly attached host the current state. Only
+				// meaningful in DISC, the only state the detector runs in.
+				if (ProtocolState == DISC)
+					TCPQueueCommandToHost(blnBusyStatus ? "BUSY TRUE" : "BUSY FALSE");
 			}
 		}
 	}
